---
// The run's machine, builds and protocol, from the data the builder wrote.
import { environment as env, toolchains as tools, protocol as p, commit, repo , text } from '@/lib/perf';
const displays = env.displays as { name: string; resolution: string; main: boolean }[];
const display = `${displays.length} × ${displays[0].name} (${displays[0].resolution})`;
const mygo = tools.mygo;
const rune = tools.rune;
---

<ul>
  <li><strong>Machine:</strong> {env.chip} ({env.machine}, {env.cores} cores, {Math.floor(env.memory_bytes / 2 ** 30)} GB), macOS {env.macos}, {env.power}.</li>
  <li><strong>Displays:</strong> {display}; the window on the main display, nothing covering it.</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Builds:</strong> zgx and GPUI Fast with their <code>dist</code> profile ({tools.rust_profile}), {tools.rust}; MyGo {mygo.mygo_version} ({mygo.mygo_commit.slice(0, 7)}, {mygo.mygo_license}) built with {mygo.go}, <code>go build {mygo.flags}</code>, cgo {mygo.cgo ? 'on' : 'off'}; Rune at {rune.rune_rev.slice(0, 8)} ({rune.rune_branch}, {rune.rune_license}), profile {rune.profile}, and a 14-line patch exposing its wheel path. Every framework uses the system allocator. zgx at <a href={`${repo}/commit/${commit}`}><code>{commit.slice(0, 7)}</code></a>.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Trials:</strong> each a fresh launch, the first {p.warmup_seconds} s discarded and the next {p.sampled_seconds} s sampled every {Math.round(p.interval_seconds * 1000)} ms; {p.repeats} trials of each mode, in alternating order, and {p.extra_trials} more of any whose CPU or GPU spread past {Math.round(p.spread_for_extra_trials * 100)}% of its median; idle {p.idle_repeats} times in the dashboard, {p.idle_window_seconds[0]}–{p.idle_window_seconds[1]} s after launch. Every trial had to run as long as asked, at 60 updates a second. Medians are shown, the trials' range beside them. Frame timing is {p.pacing_repeats} separate {p.pacing_seconds} s captures of each mode.
  </li>
</ul>
<h3 id="how-rune-is-driven">How Rune is driven</h3>
<ul set:html={text.rune_notes} />
